From 623e45e1b01540444eaaeb961d234d2179d5e7fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:53:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Wait for supervised dashboard mount before gateway
 READY

Why-chain:
- Desktop releases local API polls when the gateway publishes READY.
- On laptop-1, all 29 retained conn=local timeouts on Nov 13 clustered
  within the minute of READY across six restarts. At 13:58:49.990 PST
  READY preceded plugin mounts at 13:58:55.188..57 and the first API
  requests at 13:58:59.297, exceeding the polls' 4-8s deadlines.
- The after-READY warm-up came from 276da15e93c's lazy cold chat -q
  optimization, but supervised Desktop/service gateways need the routes.
- Start supervised warm-up just after the runtime listener, overlapping
  adapter/cron startup. The gateway-bound http_lifespan owns HTTP/PTY
  resources only and does not require running adapters.
- Await warm-up before READY and on the early-verdict path. Shield the
  task and bound the wait at 30s; warn and publish READY on timeout while
  mounting continues. Failed mounts retain first-request retry.

Idle-exit gateways still do not warm/import the dashboard before READY.
The in-process ensure already has a 300s adaptive CPU-starvation ceiling.
CLI ensure/attach instead defaulted to a hard 60s and Desktop killed its
client at 75s; align these explicit callers to 330s (300+30), retaining
Desktop's 15s output/interpreter grace and explicit --timeout overrides.
This also means a hung default explicit CLI start can now wait 330s;
callers wanting a shorter hard deadline still supply --timeout.

Proof:
- Real bootstrap with a slow mount: READY waits, bounded mount completes
  after READY, failure warns then first ASGI request retries successfully,
  early verdict awaits, and adapter start overlaps the mount.
- Baseline: four original new regressions fail; idle-exit is an unchanged
  control, killed by removing the new non-idle guard. Removing shield also
  kills the pending-mount assertion. Cold idle path leaves web_server absent.
- Focused Python suites: 54 passed, 4 platform skips; lazy listener and
  deferred integrity suites pass. All 50 direct bootstrap/listener consumer
  files pass (510 tests, 4 platform skips). The no-task and shield mutants
  each fail their behavioral assertion; restored suite passes all 10 tests.
- Desktop deadline test fails with old 60s budget; 36 Desktop tests pass
  with the fix; electron TypeScript check passes. Full scripts/check passes.

Live MacBook restart proof is separately owned by t_01a1d6fbb11b47da:
backend_cold_start.count == 0 within 45s of READY after deployment.
No live Mac restart or detector change is part of this PR.
